    "result": "PR-005 is functionally corrected for R005-1 through R005-4. It remains integration-blocked on the independently confirmed WP11 historical-input gate.\n\n**Head (pending in the handoff):** `afb90565456a429e73527f2bb99daf9cf174aa3c`  \n**Tree:** `bf49d34160b37c79a5948bc32199c24c2c92f24a`  \n**Branch:** `codex/ce-ushso-pr005-grok-r2-2026-pr005-freshness-r2-029d2d4b27dc-4eaf084b`  \n**Logical base (unchanged):** `15b351a92af729f9ba07359fd210123fdfd76bb3`  \n**Continuation execution base:** `941c9cd02a3a87c4239e6b75cdccbf4c8ec095e9`  \n**PR-004 dependency merge (unchanged):** `463f092f71c0ed1ef2aa5baa29b186e5697d04ce`\n\nOriginal three commits are retained. Additive corrections:\n\n| ID | SHA | Subject |\n|---|---|---|\n| C-005-4 | `e7cd7e69823dcaf5f95aa578dc846d02b5882821` | Correct freshness projection, trusted clock, and grain claims |\n| C-005-5 | `afb90565456a429e73527f2bb99daf9cf174aa3c` | Record PR005 freshness correction evidence |\n\nWorking tree is clean. Nothing was pushed.\n\n**Corrected behavior**\n- Search, object browse, numeric browse fallback, and dataset lookup share one `projectFreshness` contract when a request clock is present.\n- Frozen `retrieve()` without `now` still uses catalog-contract `freshnessState` (lexical/direct-base byte-parity intact).\n- Ordinary caller `Date` headers are ignored; explicit injected `now` remains for internal tests.\n- Unknown / `not_live_verified` observations are not last-successful-check evidence; explicit null attempt timestamps stay unknown through adapter, card, and detail.\n- Only `source_asserted` / `verified_first_party` grain claims render as Typical unit/Grain; inferred/unavailable values stay qualified search aids.\n\n**Checks**\n- Freshness/grain: 11 passed\n- WP1: 7 passed\n- Web: 29 files, 162 passed\n- Retrieval: 105 passed, including frozen byte-parity\n- Controller semantics replay (`pr005-independent-semantics-v3.mjs`): 10/10 cases passed; script still hardcodes `accepted=false`; source record bytes unchanged\n- Worker functional retry: 65 passed (first recording failed because semantics files were written during the CI/WP0 sealed-artifact window; that failure is retained)\n- `npm run test:worker`: **exit 1**, 342 passed / 4 failed, all in `tests/wp11-attestation.test.mjs`\n- `check-handoff`: accepted\n\n**WP11 blocker (unchanged policy)**  \nFirst reported mismatch: `apps/web/src/components/ResultCard.test.ts` actual `f80476d8ba1a0343eaceae664b0f7aa1d4312105779b1c54cd5e2d91bbd85978` expected `16226fad7dbbb87f6ca90541fcb33366b4104d8f7324e1f2373cff8446afe06d`. Pins, approvals, receipts, and gate policy were not edited. Proposed follow-up only: `verification/research-program/pr-005/evidence/c-005-4/proposed-wp11-current-input-pins.json`.\n\n**Downstream**  \nAstra re-reviews this correction head. Bind the committed head externally (`head_sha` is pending). Keep PR-005 integration-blocked until the separately reviewed WP11 current-input attestation follow-up is combined. Do not merge or deploy from this packet.",
